From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:42:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] S2: MTP first form without its head on DFlash2 rounds
 that stay on DFlash2 behind G6_MTP_HEAD_SKIP=P

A solo DFlash2 round whose next round drafts with DFlash2 again (no switch, probe, warm-up or insert) runs the MTP
first form without the lm head, local top list, merge and head collective on all but every P-th such round (the
drafter choice is made before the first form, as under G6_DRAFT_PAR). St::d1ok marks d[1] as not drafted: the drafter
choice's MTP position-1 observation skips it, demote chains from DFlash2's draft of that position, the K-stop log prints
m1ok -1. g6m4 captures head-less first-form graphs (exec_dh) and enqueues two draft collectives for them; the S2
timeline counts them as draft_nh. Drafts only. Host test batch_headskip_test (P = 1 == off; P = 4 exact, no stale
draft used, demote after a head-less round).
